From: Sreesai Arjun <sreesaiarjun@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] AP_HAL_ChibiOS: book bdshot RECV_FAILED on the channel that failed

bdshot_finish_dshot_gcr_transaction() (DMA-complete / receive-timeout ISR)
sets prev_telem_chan = curr_telem_chan and rotates curr_telem_chan to the
next input-capture channel, and only then marks the transaction
RECV_COMPLETE or RECV_FAILED.  bdshot_prepare_for_next_pulse() books
RECV_COMPLETE against group.chan[prev_telem_chan] (correct), but books
RECV_FAILED (no edges captured: the ESC never answered) against
curr_telem_chan - the NEXT channel, and as a group-local index although
erpm_errors[] is indexed by global channel number.  The index-space part
only matters on groups whose chan[] is not {0,1,2,3}.

Effect: the no-reply failures of a silent ESC inflate its neighbour's
erpm error rate, which AP_ESC_Telem logs (ESC message error_rate field)
and returns from get_raw_rpm_and_error_rate().  The silent ESC itself
never publishes a rate (update_rpm() is only called on a valid eRPM), so
the log points at the wrong motor.

Once failures are booked on the silent channel it never reaches the
RECV_COMPLETE branch that holds the 5 s statistics reset, so the reset is
applied in the RECV_FAILED branch as well; otherwise the uint16 counter
grows until it wraps (~164 s at 400 Hz per motor) and the first rate
published after the ESC recovers is stale.

The diagnosis comes from reading RCOutput_bdshot.cpp; the counter logic
before and after this change is reproduced in a host-side model
(Nano H743 AIO repo, firmware/bdshot_telem, test T8), not on hardware.

---
--- a/libraries/AP_HAL_ChibiOS/RCOutput_bdshot.cpp
+++ b/libraries/AP_HAL_ChibiOS/RCOutput_bdshot.cpp
@@ -284,7 +284,20 @@
             _bdshot.erpm_last_stats_ms[chan] = now;
         }
     } else if (group.dshot_state == DshotState::RECV_FAILED) {
-        _bdshot.erpm_errors[group.bdshot.curr_telem_chan]++;
+        // bdshot_finish_dshot_gcr_transaction() has already rotated
+        // curr_telem_chan to the next channel, so the channel that failed to
+        // answer is prev_telem_chan; erpm_errors[] is indexed by global
+        // channel number, as in the RECV_COMPLETE branch above.
+        const uint8_t chan = group.chan[group.bdshot.prev_telem_chan];
+        const uint32_t now = AP_HAL::millis();
+        _bdshot.erpm_errors[chan]++;
+        // a silent ESC never reaches RECV_COMPLETE, so apply the same 5 s
+        // statistics window here or its uint16 counter grows until it wraps
+        if (now - _bdshot.erpm_last_stats_ms[chan] > 5000) {
+            _bdshot.erpm_clean_frames[chan] = 0;
+            _bdshot.erpm_errors[chan] = 0;
+            _bdshot.erpm_last_stats_ms[chan] = now;
+        }
     }
 
     if (group.bdshot.enabled) {
